---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---

<Site
	title="About"
	section="about"
	description="Where Solmara's name comes from, and how it is made."
	eyebrow="About"
	heading="The sun's nightmare"
>
	<section class="name">
		<h2>The name</h2>
		<p><em>Sol</em> is the sun. <em>Mara</em> is the spirit of Nordic folklore who sits on a sleeper's chest, the <em>mare</em> in <em>nightmare</em>. Solmara is the sun's nightmare: an eclipse, when the wolf that chases the sun across the sky catches it.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="facts">
		<div>
			<h3>Mac, Windows and Linux</h3>
			<p>The same studio on all three. Start a song on one and finish it on another.</p>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h3>Projects you can trust</h3>
			<p>Saved as readable text, so a version history shows what changed, and brought back after a crash.</p>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h3>Devices with names of their own</h3>
			<p>Where a device is modeled on a piece of gear, it has its own name and face. Our own designs have Nordic names.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="help">
		<h2>Found a problem, or have an idea?</h2>
		<p>Tell us on <a href="https://github.com/mattias800/solmara/issues/new/choose">GitHub</a>: what you did, what you heard, and what you expected.</p>
	</section>
</Site>
